      "sourceTextSha256": "5d7506bbf03e5b29bdf1d374f56c5fdcc6df45499da75635887ece960adffbd0",
      "text": "Day 14 · Full-day excursion to Valparaíso and Viña del Mar, through the olive groves, orchards and vineyards of the Curacaví and Casablanca valleys (about 120 km, 1.5 hours). Valparaíso spreads across 42 hills, famous for its distinctive architecture and listed as a UNESCO World Heritage Site, its levels linked by historic funiculars, stairways and paths. Visit Sotomayor Square and the historic Naval Headquarters, then walk the Gervasoni and Atkinson promenades on Cerro Concepción, with a magnificent view of the port. Visit Pablo Neruda’s house, La Sebastiana, then Viña del Mar, the “Garden City”: the Flower Clock, Reñaca Beach, the waterfront and the Fonck Museum.\n\nAccommodation: Mandarin Oriental Santiago, Club Room, breakfast",
